cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this container, please cite it as below. It packages the FaMAF CVA6
  Project's additions on top of gem5, which is cited under references along with
  its papers.
title: "FaMAF CVA6 Project: the gem5 container"
abstract: >-
  A Docker image holding gem5 v25.0.0.1 built three times, with the MinorCPU
  configuration matched to the CORE-V CVA6 for a thesis at FaMAF, Universidad
  Nacional de Cordoba, on how closely a gem5 MinorCPU configuration can be made
  to match a real RISC-V core. It ships the stock and patched builds and a third
  for working on the patch, the MinorCPU patch itself, the matched
  configurations and their calibration harness, the calibration and teaching
  benchmark sets, the run drivers and sweeps, and the MinorFlow pipeline viewer.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Nieto"
    given-names: "Manuel"
    affiliation: "FaMAF, Universidad Nacional de Córdoba"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3893-5628"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/FaMAF-CVA6-Project/CVA6/blob/master/dockerfiles/gem5/LICENSE.FaMAF"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FaMAF-CVA6-Project/CVA6"
url: "https://hub.docker.com/r/manuel313/famaf_gem5"
keywords:
  - RISC-V
  - gem5
  - MinorCPU
  - CVA6
  - computer architecture
  - microarchitecture
  - simulator calibration
  - Docker
